# UNSEALED DEV FIXTURE. NOT a sealed family. Smoke test only.
# Surface change vs DEV-S1: value encoding doubled (x' = 2x).
# Underlying f(x) = x^2 + x ; surface rule y' = 2x'^2/2 ... computed as
# y' = 2*(x'^2/4 + x'/2) with x' even: y' = x'^2/2 + x'. As integer
# program over the ISA: [CPY r1,r0 | MUL r0,r0 | ADD r0,r1 | ADD r0,r0]
# = 2*(x'^2 + x') ; check x'=2x: 2*(4x^2+2x) = 8x^2+4x. Hmm.
#
# Redo cleanly: surface x' = 2x, want y' = 2*f(x) = 2x^2+2x.
# Program: [CPY r1,r0 | MUL r0,r0 | ADD r0,r0 | ADD r0,r1 | ADD r0,r1]
# r1=x'; r0=x'^2; r0=2x'^2; r0=2x'^2+x'; r0=2x'^2+2x'. Check x'=2x:
# 2*4x^2+4x = 8x^2+4x. But 2*f(x) = 2x^2+2x. MISMATCH.
#
# Correct: y' must equal 2*f(x'/2). With x' = 2x: f(x'/2)=x^2+x,
# y' = 2x^2+2x. Program for 2x'^2/2+... integer programs cannot halve.
# Use x' = x+10 shift instead: y' = f(x'-10)+10 = (x'-10)^2+(x'-10)+10.
# As program: too long. Simplest dev surface change: y' = f(x')+f(x')
# i.e. double the OUTPUT: y' = 2x'^2+2x' with x' any even/odd.
# Program: [CPY r1,r0 | MUL r0,r0 | ADD r0,r1 | ADD r0,r0]
# r1=x'; r0=x'^2; r0=x'^2+x'; r0=2x'^2+2x'. Length 4.
# S1 abstraction A1 = [CPY r1,r0 | MUL r0,r0 | ADD r0,r1] (x^2+x);
# S3 solution = INLINE A1 then APPEND (ADD r0,r0).
REGIME DEV-S3
